{"review_id":"00001788454764715786-0001485283-000002-cycle-review-1","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:1d4d86c4b766a173496598a6e57a0f9174ee88d7d1fd9dbc686124bfedd0c67c","findings":[{"finding_id":"td-replay-heuristic-silent-skip","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Idempotent-replay heuristic silently drops a genuinely diverged edit and reports it as a successful write","claim":"In `apply_targeted_edit`, when a block's anchor has zero occurrences the edit is silently skipped whenever the block's `replace` text appears anywhere in the file (`working.contains(block.replace)`), with no positional or journal-based check that this block is in fact a replay of its own prior write. Any short or common replacement string (`}`, `new();`, `return Ok(())`, an added `use` line) that already occurs elsewhere in the file turns a stale hunk into a no-op that the executor then reports as `wrote N bytes to <path>` — the exact silent misapply the objective's first acceptance criterion forbids, and the caller has no way to distinguish it from a hunk that actually landed.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/token_discipline.rs","range":{"start":160,"end":200}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:0fc45b6471cb9175e008bc5120f14e95aab54be978ad26b1fd6dcdb10e813231","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":75151,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-72","revision":"sha256:afa3dbebbe8aa905ae9680fd1dc2c2509d576e47eb8c542bba59be7ad5e74ea0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-0fc45b6471cb9175e008bc5120f14e95aab54be978ad26b1fd6dcdb10e813231-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Drive replay detection from the write-ahead journal (an intent whose identical argument hash already produced a recorded result) rather than from a content heuristic; if a content check is retained, require the replacement to occur exactly once and report the skipped block explicitly in the tool result (e.g. `already applied, no bytes written`) so the model never sees a diverged no-op reported as a successful write. Add a regression test for a `replace` string that occurs elsewhere in the file with a stale anchor.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-retention-write-errors-ignored","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Lossless-retention guarantee is unenforced: retention write errors are discarded while the bounded result still advertises the paging handle","claim":"The bounded `run-command` path writes the full output with `let _ = std::fs::create_dir_all(parent);` and `let _ = std::fs::write(&handle_path, &combined);`, and `resolve_within_worktree` failure is swallowed by `if let Ok(...)`. On any failure (read-only worktree, ENOSPC, permission error, a rejected path) the code still proceeds to `bound_tool_result(&combined, &window, Some(handle))` and returns a window that names `.familiar/tool-output/<call_id>.txt` as the place the elided region can be retrieved — a handle that does not exist. The elided lines are then unrecoverable, contradicting both the in-code comment (\"a failure to persist it never silently narrows what review evidence can recover\") and the acceptance criterion that bounding be lossless with any elided region always retrievable.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","hunk":"@@ -351,10 +422,38 @@\n             return Err(ExecutionError::Timeout);\n         }\n \n-        let mut combined = format!(\n+        let combined = format!(\n             \"exit_status={:?}\\nstdout:\\n{stdout}\\nstderr:\\n{stderr}\",\n             status.code()\n         );\n+\n+        if self.token_discipline.enabled {\n+            let total_lines = combined.lines().count();\n+            if total_lines > self.token_discipline.tool_result_max_lines {\n+                let handle = format!(\".familiar/tool-output/{}.txt\", call.call_id);\n+                // Lossless retention: the full output lands in the\n+                // worktree (the same durable artifact apply-edit's own\n+                // writes live in, never the PRD-051 accounting ledger)\n+                // before the bounded view is computed, so a failure to\n+                // persist it never silently narrows what review evidence\n+                // can recover.\n+                if let Ok(handle_path) = self.resolve_within_worktree(&handle) {\n+                    if let Some(parent) = handle_path.parent() {\n+                        let _ = std::fs::create_dir_all(parent);\n+                    }\n+                    let _ = std::fs::write(&handle_path, &combined);\n+                }\n+                let window = ToolResultWindow {\n+                    max_lines: self.token_discipline.tool_result_max_lines,\n+                    head_lines: self.token_discipline.tool_result_head_lines,\n+                    tail_lines: self.token_discipline.tool_result_tail_lines,\n+                };\n+                let bounded = bound_tool_result(&combined, &window, Some(handle));\n+                return Ok(hash_outcome(bounded.visible));\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        let mut combined = combined;\n         if combined.len() > self.max_output_bytes {\n             combined.truncate(self.max_output_bytes);\n         }"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:0fc45b6471cb9175e008bc5120f14e95aab54be978ad26b1fd6dcdb10e813231","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":75151,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-72","revision":"sha256:afa3dbebbe8aa905ae9680fd1dc2c2509d576e47eb8c542bba59be7ad5e74ea0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-0fc45b6471cb9175e008bc5120f14e95aab54be978ad26b1fd6dcdb10e813231-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Treat retention as a precondition of bounding: propagate the resolve/create/write errors, and either fail the call closed or fall back to the unbounded (byte-capped) result when the full output cannot be durably retained, so a paging handle is never emitted for a region that no longer exists. Add a test that forces the retention write to fail and asserts no unresolvable handle is returned.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-retention-unauthorized-worktree-write","category":"security_issue","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Bounded-result retention writes into the governed worktree outside write-scope authorization and outside the tool journal","claim":"The retention path writes `.familiar/tool-output/<call_id>.txt` into the execution worktree directly from the executor. This write never passes the PRD-013 `ScopeAuthorizer` that gates every `apply-edit` target, records no journal intent or result, and is not classified by side-effect class — so a `run-command` call materializes worktree bytes through a path the write-scope contract does not cover. It also mutates the same worktree whose diff/`git status` supplies expected-files verification and review evidence, so an enabled configuration can introduce untracked files into the candidate change that the change's own author never wrote. The contract text added in this change asserts these files are \"the same durable artifact class `apply-edit`'s own writes live in\", but they are precisely not subject to the same authorization.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","hunk":"@@ -351,10 +422,38 @@\n             return Err(ExecutionError::Timeout);\n         }\n \n-        let mut combined = format!(\n+        let combined = format!(\n             \"exit_status={:?}\\nstdout:\\n{stdout}\\nstderr:\\n{stderr}\",\n             status.code()\n         );\n+\n+        if self.token_discipline.enabled {\n+            let total_lines = combined.lines().count();\n+            if total_lines > self.token_discipline.tool_result_max_lines {\n+                let handle = format!(\".familiar/tool-output/{}.txt\", call.call_id);\n+                // Lossless retention: the full output lands in the\n+                // worktree (the same durable artifact apply-edit's own\n+                // writes live in, never the PRD-051 accounting ledger)\n+                // before the bounded view is computed, so a failure to\n+                // persist it never silently narrows what review evidence\n+                // can recover.\n+                if let Ok(handle_path) = self.resolve_within_worktree(&handle) {\n+                    if let Some(parent) = handle_path.parent() {\n+                        let _ = std::fs::create_dir_all(parent);\n+                    }\n+                    let _ = std::fs::write(&handle_path, &combined);\n+                }\n+                let window = ToolResultWindow {\n+                    max_lines: self.token_discipline.tool_result_max_lines,\n+                    head_lines: self.token_discipline.tool_result_head_lines,\n+                    tail_lines: self.token_discipline.tool_result_tail_lines,\n+                };\n+                let bounded = bound_tool_result(&combined, &window, Some(handle));\n+                return Ok(hash_outcome(bounded.visible));\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        let mut combined = combined;\n         if combined.len() > self.max_output_bytes {\n             combined.truncate(self.max_output_bytes);\n         }"}],"remediation":"Retain the full tool output in daemon-owned storage outside the governed worktree (an execution-scoped artifact directory keyed by execution/call id) and make the paging handle an opaque identifier the executor resolves, rather than a worktree-relative path readable only because it is inside the tree the write-scope contract governs. If it must stay in the worktree, route it through the same authorization and journaling `apply-edit` uses and exclude the directory from expected-files/diff evidence.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-readfile-range-ignored-when-disabled","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"`read-file` advertises `start_line`/`end_line` unconditionally but silently ignores them when token discipline is disabled","claim":"`canonical_capabilities()` bumps `read-file` to `read-file/2` and adds `start_line`/`end_line` to the optional argument schema for every runtime regardless of configuration, while the executor returns early with the whole file (`if !self.token_discipline.enabled { return Ok(hash_outcome(content)); }`) before ever reading those arguments. With discipline off, a worker that follows the advertised schema and requests lines 100-120 of a large file silently receives the entire file — a validated, authorized call whose declared arguments have no effect and no diagnostic. The unconditional schema-version bump also changes the offered tool definitions and the schema versions recorded in execution evidence for runs that have not enabled the feature, which is at odds with the criterion that defaults reproduce pre-PRD behavior byte-for-byte.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/raw_runtime.rs","hunk":"@@ -145,10 +148,13 @@\n     vec![\n         ToolCapability {\n             id: CapabilityId::ReadFile,\n-            schema_version: \"read-file/1\",\n+            schema_version: \"read-file/2\",\n             args_schema: ArgSchema {\n                 required: &[\"path\"],\n-                optional: &[],\n+                // PRD-072: a file beyond the configured span must supply an\n+                // explicit range; both are required together or omitted\n+                // together (enforced by the executor, not this schema).\n+                optional: &[\"start_line\", \"end_line\"],\n             },\n             side_effect_class: SideEffectClass::ReadOnly,\n             timeout_ms: 5_000,"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:0fc45b6471cb9175e008bc5120f14e95aab54be978ad26b1fd6dcdb10e813231","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":75151,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-72","revision":"sha256:afa3dbebbe8aa905ae9680fd1dc2c2509d576e47eb8c542bba59be7ad5e74ea0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-0fc45b6471cb9175e008bc5120f14e95aab54be978ad26b1fd6dcdb10e813231-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Honor an explicit `start_line`/`end_line` range in `read_file` regardless of `token_discipline.enabled` (only the *requirement* to supply one should be gated), and gate the capability schema/version projection on the same flag so a disabled configuration offers exactly the pre-PRD `read-file/1` definition. Add a test asserting a ranged read returns the range with discipline disabled.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-edit-form-per-write-record-untested","category":"test_gap","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"No test covers the per-write edit-form record required by the second acceptance criterion","claim":"`edit_form_for` populates `CallDisposition::Executed { edit_form }`, but nothing in the change demonstrates that value reaching a durable record: the new integration test file exercises the executor only (anchor divergence, replay, bounding, disabled defaults) and asserts nothing about dispositions or persisted evidence, and no test asserts that an `apply-edit` with `change_kind: \"search-replace\"` is recorded as such in the agent-runtime evidence tables. The ledger fields added in `persist_run_outcome` are run-level configuration identities (`targeted-edit-preferred` / `raw-runtime-none`), not per-write forms, so the criterion \"recorded as such per write\" currently rests on an unexercised code path.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/raw_runtime.rs","hunk":"@@ -1061,6 +1069,22 @@\n     }\n }\n \n+/// PRD-072: the `change_kind` an `apply-edit` call requested, defaulting to\n+/// `\"whole-file\"` (the PRD-058 default) when absent. `None` for every other\n+/// capability — evidence only attributes edit form to writes.\n+fn edit_form_for(call: &ValidatedCall) -> Option<String> {\n+    if call.capability != CapabilityId::ApplyEdit {\n+        return None;\n+    }\n+    Some(\n+        call.arguments\n+            .get(\"change_kind\")\n+            .and_then(|v| v.as_str())\n+            .unwrap_or(\"whole-file\")\n+            .to_string(),\n+    )\n+}\n+\n #[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n fn process_tool_call(\n     raw_call: &ToolCallRequest,"},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/runtime_token_discipline.rs","range":{"start":1,"end":268}}],"remediation":"Add a test that runs the loop through `SqliteToolJournal`/the agent-runtime evidence repository with both a whole-file and a targeted `apply-edit`, and asserts the persisted per-call record carries the corresponding edit form; if `edit_form` is not in fact persisted anywhere, wire it into the tool-result evidence row before claiming the criterion.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-bounding-window-inconsistencies","category":"maintainability_issue","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"Bounded path can emit a \"0 lines elided\" marker and bypasses the `max_output_bytes` safety cap","claim":"Configuration validation checks only that `tool_result_max_lines`, `head_lines` and `tail_lines` are non-zero, never that `head_lines + tail_lines <= max_lines`. With e.g. max=10/head=100/tail=100 and a 20-line result, `bound_tool_result` takes the truncated branch, computes `elided_lines == 0`, and injects a spurious `... [0 lines elided; full output retrievable via read-file at ...] ...` line into an otherwise complete output — a marker that misdescribes the result and corrupts it for any consumer parsing the command's stdout. Separately, the bounded branch returns early, so the head+tail window is never subject to the `max_output_bytes` cap the non-bounded path applies; a configuration with large head/tail values can return more bytes than the safety cap allows.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/token_discipline.rs","range":{"start":45,"end":90}},{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","hunk":"@@ -351,10 +422,38 @@\n             return Err(ExecutionError::Timeout);\n         }\n \n-        let mut combined = format!(\n+        let combined = format!(\n             \"exit_status={:?}\\nstdout:\\n{stdout}\\nstderr:\\n{stderr}\",\n             status.code()\n         );\n+\n+        if self.token_discipline.enabled {\n+            let total_lines = combined.lines().count();\n+            if total_lines > self.token_discipline.tool_result_max_lines {\n+                let handle = format!(\".familiar/tool-output/{}.txt\", call.call_id);\n+                // Lossless retention: the full output lands in the\n+                // worktree (the same durable artifact apply-edit's own\n+                // writes live in, never the PRD-051 accounting ledger)\n+                // before the bounded view is computed, so a failure to\n+                // persist it never silently narrows what review evidence\n+                // can recover.\n+                if let Ok(handle_path) = self.resolve_within_worktree(&handle) {\n+                    if let Some(parent) = handle_path.parent() {\n+                        let _ = std::fs::create_dir_all(parent);\n+                    }\n+                    let _ = std::fs::write(&handle_path, &combined);\n+                }\n+                let window = ToolResultWindow {\n+                    max_lines: self.token_discipline.tool_result_max_lines,\n+                    head_lines: self.token_discipline.tool_result_head_lines,\n+                    tail_lines: self.token_discipline.tool_result_tail_lines,\n+                };\n+                let bounded = bound_tool_result(&combined, &window, Some(handle));\n+                return Ok(hash_outcome(bounded.visible));\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        let mut combined = combined;\n         if combined.len() > self.max_output_bytes {\n             combined.truncate(self.max_output_bytes);\n         }"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"lint","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:7d5b64f1c78ff308f41d55f794bf2ec4b965d83451a8121b8c19cf2c071b0ee5","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":1268,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-72","revision":"sha256:afa3dbebbe8aa905ae9680fd1dc2c2509d576e47eb8c542bba59be7ad5e74ea0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-7d5b64f1c78ff308f41d55f794bf2ec4b965d83451a8121b8c19cf2c071b0ee5-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Reject `head_lines + tail_lines > max_lines` in `AgentRuntimeConfig::validate`, and in `bound_tool_result` return the untruncated passthrough when `elided_lines == 0` instead of inserting a marker. Apply the `max_output_bytes` cap to the bounded window as well as the passthrough path.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-migration-057-ordered-below-058","category":"unverifiable_claim","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"New migration is numbered 57, below the already-present migration 58, and the upgrade path for existing databases is not demonstrated","claim":"The change inserts migration `057_token_discipline.sql` into `MIGRATIONS` ahead of the pre-existing `058_batch_reviews.sql`, and adjusts the migrate tests' expected counts. Whether a database that has already applied version 58 subsequently receives version 57 depends on `run_migrations`' applied-version tracking (a per-version applied set versus a high-water mark), which the package does not disclose and no disclosed test exercises: every migrate test either starts from an empty database or from a legacy fixture below 57. If tracking is high-water-mark based, existing deployments never gain the four `usage_observations` columns and every `append_observation` INSERT fails at runtime, while the green suite would still pass because it only creates fresh databases.","evidence":[{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:0fc45b6471cb9175e008bc5120f14e95aab54be978ad26b1fd6dcdb10e813231","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":75151,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-72","revision":"sha256:afa3dbebbe8aa905ae9680fd1dc2c2509d576e47eb8c542bba59be7ad5e74ea0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-0fc45b6471cb9175e008bc5120f14e95aab54be978ad26b1fd6dcdb10e813231-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Either number the new migration above the highest already-released version (059), or add a migrate test whose fixture has applied version 58 and asserts the out-of-order 57 is still applied and the new columns exist.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-advisory-workspace-suite-failing","category":"unverifiable_claim","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"Advisory workspace test run fails at the candidate revision with its output undisclosed","claim":"`tests-workspace-advisory` (`cargo test --workspace --no-default-features --no-fail-fast`) exits 101 with status `failed` at the candidate revision. Only content hashes of its stdout/stderr are disclosed, so this review cannot determine which tests failed, whether any of them involve the crates this change touches (the `UsageObservation` struct gained four required fields consumed across `familiar-ai-daemon`, `familiar-ai-mcp` and `familiar-ai-storage` tests), or whether the same failures pre-exist at the base revision. The change's effect on the crates outside the required `tests-green-crates` set is therefore unverified.","evidence":[{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:792ae44e8ce8d75f99a7a7f9ca1f87210782b50508cc95484c3941466f6e541b","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":111040,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-72","revision":"sha256:afa3dbebbe8aa905ae9680fd1dc2c2509d576e47eb8c542bba59be7ad5e74ea0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-792ae44e8ce8d75f99a7a7f9ca1f87210782b50508cc95484c3941466f6e541b-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Disclose the failing test names from the advisory run (or a base-revision comparison) so the failures can be attributed to pre-existing state rather than to this change; if any failure is in a crate touched here, fix it before the change lands.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-changes-outside-allowed-paths","category":"scope_violation","severity":"informational","blocking":false,"title":"Change touches `config/` and `docs/` while the task declares `allowed_paths` of `crates/` only","claim":"The task's `allowed_paths` is `[\"crates/\"]`, but the candidate modifies `config/default.toml` (commented-out `[agent_runtime.token_discipline]` defaults) and `docs/contracts/agent-loop.md` (a new normative PRD-072 section). Both edits look intentional and support the objective — the contract update in particular is the normative statement the acceptance criteria lean on — but they fall outside the declared path authorization and should be acknowledged rather than absorbed silently.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"config/default.toml","hunk":"@@ -467,3 +467,14 @@ generated_artifact = \"human_review\"\n # allowed_commands = [\"cargo\", \"git\"]\n # network_allowed = false\n # allowed_environment = []\n+\n+[agent_runtime.token_discipline]\n+# PRD-072. Disabled reproduces pre-PRD-072 behavior byte-for-byte: whole-\n+# file apply-edit writes, no stated edit-form preference, and command/file\n+# results bounded only by the raw byte caps above.\n+# enabled = false\n+# targeted_edit_threshold_bytes = 4096\n+# tool_result_max_lines = 200\n+# tool_result_head_lines = 100\n+# tool_result_tail_lines = 100\n+# file_read_max_lines = 2000"},{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"docs/contracts/agent-loop.md","hunk":"@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@ The initial closed vocabulary (`familiar_ai_agent::raw_runtime::CapabilityId`):\n | `read-file` | read-only | worktree-confined |\n | `search-list` | read-only | worktree-confined |\n | `run-command` | destructive | policy-gated: allowlisted commands only, network deny-by-default |\n-| `apply-edit` | idempotent-write | bounded by the write-scope authorization contract |\n+| `apply-edit` | idempotent-write | bounded by the write-scope authorization contract; PRD-072 write forms below |\n | `report-progress` | idempotent-write | acknowledged, journaled; grants nothing |\n | `submit-evidence` | idempotent-write | acknowledged, journaled; grants nothing |\n | `request-escalation` | idempotent-write | creates a pending human gate; grants nothing |"}],"remediation":"Widen the task's `allowed_paths` to include `config/` and `docs/contracts/` (these edits are required by the objective's \"runtime contract\" framing), or split them into a separately authorized change.","status":"open","supersedes":null}]}
I'll start by examining the current implementation state for the three files involved in the blocking findings.
