## Findings

**1. No `artifact_dir`/`state_dir`-style field exists on daemon-side tool-executor structs**, but `AppPaths` (`crates/familiar-ai-core/src/paths.rs:8-16`) already carries `config_dir`, `data_dir`, `state_dir`, `runtime_dir`, `log_dir` — computed via XDG env vars with `dirs::home_dir()` fallback (`paths.rs:147-199`, linux; macOS variant follows). This is the one and only "outside-worktree root" convention in the codebase.

**2. `review-artifacts` is just `data_dir.join("review-artifacts")`**, computed inline at the call site — `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/run.rs:2413`:
```rust
let artifact_directory = paths.data_dir.join("review-artifacts");
```
fed into `GitEvidenceCollector::new(artifact_directory, ...)` (`run.rs:2415`, collector defined in `crates/familiar-ai-review/src/evidence.rs:29-37`). There's a sibling pattern at `run.rs:2045/2081/2746-2750`: `capture_worktree_baseline(worktree, data_dir, execution_id)` writes `data_dir.join(format!("review-baseline-{execution_id}.index"))` — i.e., an **execution_id-keyed file directly under `data_dir`**, no dedicated subdirectory-per-execution abstraction. Similarly `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/plan.rs:456` uses `paths.state_dir.join("planner-artifacts")`. `crates/familiar-ai-review/src/verification.rs:40-47` (`ArtifactVerification` or similar) takes an arbitrary `artifact_directory: PathBuf` in its constructor — same shape as `GitEvidenceCollector`.

**3. `SandboxedToolExecutor`** (`crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs:185-193`) has fields: `worktree_root`, `sandbox`, `command_timeout_ms`, `max_output_bytes`, `token_discipline`. **No filesystem root besides `worktree_root`.** Importantly, it has **zero production call sites** — `lib.rs` only re-exports it, and it's constructed only in test files (`tests/openai_adapter.rs`, `tests/raw_runtime.rs`, `tests/runtime_token_discipline.rs`, `tests/xai_adapter.rs`) as direct struct literals. It is not yet wired into `run.rs` or `drive.rs`. This means whoever wires it up (this PRD, presumably) has a free hand — no existing call site needs updating, only the eventual integration point.

**4. No existing per-execution artifact/scratch abstraction to reuse** — the closest are `GitEvidenceCollector`/verification's `artifact_directory: PathBuf` constructor param and the ad hoc `review-baseline-{execution_id}.index` filename convention in `run.rs`. Neither is exposed to `agent_runtime.rs`; both are constructed at the `run.rs` orchestration layer using `paths.data_dir`.

## Recommendation

Add an `AppPaths`-style directory (e.g. `paths.data_dir.join("tool-output")` or reuse `review-artifacts`) computed once at the `run.rs` orchestration layer — same place `artifact_directory` for `GitEvidenceCollector` is already built (`run.rs:2413`) — then pass it into `SandboxedToolExecutor` as a new field (e.g. `tool_output_dir: PathBuf`), keyed by `execution_id` subdirectory (mirroring the `review-baseline-{execution_id}` naming already in use). This requires no new config plumbing: `AppPaths::data_dir` is already resolved and passed around every call site that builds daemon components, so it is trivially reachable at the point `SandboxedToolExecutor` will be constructed. Since there are no production callers yet, adding the field is a pure addition, not a breaking change to existing wiring.
