{"review_id":"00001788454764715786-0001485283-000002-cycle-review-3","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:309ce441b5d28db425ef8ec15b81a08366a7d08016661902edbf281704d45992","findings":[{"finding_id":"td-applyedit-schema-omits-change-kind","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"apply-edit's canonical capability schema never declares `change_kind`, so targeted edits are unreachable through the validated loop","claim":"The change teaches `SandboxedToolExecutor::apply_edit` to read a `change_kind` argument and select a targeted edit form, but `canonical_capabilities()` was updated only for `read-file` — its `schema_version` was bumped to `read-file/2` and `optional` widened to `[\"start_line\", \"end_line\"]` precisely because a new optional argument must be declared there. `apply-edit`'s `ToolCapability` is untouched: its `schema_version` is not bumped and `change_kind` appears in neither `required` nor `optional`. Per the agent-loop contract, every tool call is validated against the canonical capability schema before anything else happens, and provider/MCP tool definitions are projections of that schema which MUST NOT widen it. So on the real path either (a) the validator rejects the undeclared `change_kind` argument and no targeted edit ever reaches the executor, or (b) it is accepted but never advertised in the projected tool definition, in which case a model has no way to learn the argument exists and the parallel `read-file` schema edit was pointless. The new regression test cannot catch this because `runtime_token_discipline.rs` constructs `ValidatedCall` structs by hand and calls `executor.execute` directly, bypassing validation and projection entirely; no test drives `run_loop` with a `change_kind` tool call.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/raw_runtime.rs","hunk":"@@ -145,10 +145,13 @@ pub fn canonical_capabilities() -> Vec<ToolCapability> {\n     vec![\n         ToolCapability {\n             id: CapabilityId::ReadFile,\n-            schema_version: \"read-file/1\",\n+            schema_version: \"read-file/2\",\n             args_schema: ArgSchema {\n                 required: &[\"path\"],\n-                optional: &[],\n+                // PRD-072: a file beyond the configured span must supply an\n+                // explicit range; both are required together or omitted\n+                // together (enforced by the executor, not this schema).\n+                optional: &[\"start_line\", \"end_line\"],\n             },\n             side_effect_class: SideEffectClass::ReadOnly,\n             timeout_ms: 5_000,"},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/runtime_token_discipline.rs","range":{"start":30,"end":45}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e49bba884b456c5679ef7d301f615bae30cd474742a401bbcb30b9774f828160","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":75574,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-72","revision":"sha256:adfc1736954048d8d1721dca2833b5c983190caffd732fa102699977cf43f088","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e49bba884b456c5679ef7d301f615bae30cd474742a401bbcb30b9774f828160-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Bump `apply-edit`'s `schema_version` and add `change_kind` to its `ArgSchema.optional` list in `canonical_capabilities()`, exactly as was done for `read-file`, and add a regression test that drives a `change_kind: \"search-replace\"` call through `run_loop`/validation (not a hand-built `ValidatedCall`) so the validated and projected paths are covered.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-worker-instruction-never-emitted","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"The targeted-edit worker instruction and its size threshold have no consumer anywhere in the change","claim":"Acceptance criterion 2 requires that \"the runtime's worker instructions state the targeted-edit preference for files above a configured size\". The change adds `token_discipline::targeted_edit_worker_instruction(threshold_bytes)` and the `targeted_edit_threshold_bytes` config field (defaulted, validated as non-zero when discipline is enabled, and documented in `config/default.toml` and the agent-loop contract), but nothing in the diff ever calls that function or reads that field on any production path. `targeted_edit_threshold_bytes` appears only in the config struct, its default/validation, and a test fixture; `targeted_edit_worker_instruction` appears only at its own definition and in its own unit test asserting the string contains \"4096\". No prompt-composition or worker-instruction code is touched by this change, so no worker is ever told the preference exists, and the configured threshold has no effect on any behavior. The lint check cannot surface this: it is run with `-A dead-code`, and a `pub` item in a library crate never triggers that lint regardless.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/token_discipline.rs","range":{"start":255,"end":275}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/agent_runtime.rs","range":{"start":95,"end":135}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e49bba884b456c5679ef7d301f615bae30cd474742a401bbcb30b9774f828160","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":75574,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-72","revision":"sha256:adfc1736954048d8d1721dca2833b5c983190caffd732fa102699977cf43f088","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e49bba884b456c5679ef7d301f615bae30cd474742a401bbcb30b9774f828160-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Wire `targeted_edit_worker_instruction(config.targeted_edit_threshold_bytes)` into the raw runtime's composed worker instructions when `token_discipline.enabled`, and add a test asserting the instruction text is present in the composed prompt when enabled and absent when disabled (so the byte-for-byte default is also covered).","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-unified-diff-substring-anchor","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Line-oriented unified-diff hunks are matched as bare substrings, so a diverged file can be silently misapplied","claim":"`parse_unified_diff_blocks` converts each hunk into a `SearchReplaceBlock` whose `search` is the context+removed lines joined with \"\\n\", and `apply_targeted_edit` then locates that anchor with `str::matches`/`replacen` — plain substring matching with no line-boundary anchoring. A hunk is line-oriented by definition, so an anchor whose first line is a suffix of a longer line in the current file matches at a non-line boundary and applies silently. Concretely, a hunk with context line `    return x;` followed by removed line `}` produces the anchor `\"    return x;\\n}\"`, which occurs exactly once inside a file whose actual line is `        return x;` (deeper indentation) followed by `}`. The occurrence count is 1, so the block applies, splicing the replacement into the middle of a line and leaving the four leading spaces stranded — the file has genuinely diverged from the hunk's context, which acceptance criterion 1 requires be rejected with a diagnostic naming the divergence, \"never a silent misapply\". The same holds at the tail of the anchor (matching a prefix of a longer line). Every unit and integration test for the unified-diff form uses anchors that happen to align with line boundaries, so the passing suite does not exercise this.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/token_discipline.rs","range":{"start":110,"end":165}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/token_discipline.rs","range":{"start":180,"end":250}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e49bba884b456c5679ef7d301f615bae30cd474742a401bbcb30b9774f828160","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":75574,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-72","revision":"sha256:adfc1736954048d8d1721dca2833b5c983190caffd732fa102699977cf43f088","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e49bba884b456c5679ef7d301f615bae30cd474742a401bbcb30b9774f828160-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"For the unified-diff form, match anchors against whole lines: require the match to begin at a line start and end at a line end (or end of file) — e.g. operate on a `Vec<&str>` of lines and search for the anchor as a contiguous line slice — and count occurrences the same way. Add a regression test where the hunk's anchor occurs only as a mid-line substring and assert `AnchorDivergence` rather than a write.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-journal-not-lossless","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Only the bounded window is hashed into the journal; the full output is retained outside any evidence store","claim":"Acceptance criterion 5 requires that bounding be \"lossless to the journal — the full untruncated tool output is durably retained for verification and review evidence even when the model sees a window\". When a `run-command` result is bounded, `run_command` returns `hash_outcome(bounded.visible)`, so the write-ahead journal's result record hashes only the head+tail window the model saw; the full output's content hash is never computed and the journal carries no reference of any kind to the retained bytes. The retained copy lives at a path derived from `std::env::temp_dir()` (see `tool_output_retention_dir`) that no journal row, evidence row, or accounting row names, and that the executor itself can only recompute while the same process, worktree root, and execution id are in play. A reviewer reconstructing the execution from the journal therefore has a hash of a truncated view and no way to reach the untruncated output; nothing about the retained file is durable in the sense the criterion requires, since `/tmp` is cleared on reboot and is tmpfs on many hosts.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","range":{"start":636,"end":679}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","range":{"start":309,"end":358}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e49bba884b456c5679ef7d301f615bae30cd474742a401bbcb30b9774f828160","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":75574,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-72","revision":"sha256:adfc1736954048d8d1721dca2833b5c983190caffd732fa102699977cf43f088","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e49bba884b456c5679ef7d301f615bae30cd474742a401bbcb30b9774f828160-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Record the full output's content hash and a durable storage reference on the tool-result journal row when a result is bounded (a hash of `combined` alongside the hash of `bounded.visible`), and retain the bytes in the daemon's durable artifact store rather than `std::env::temp_dir()`. Add a test asserting the journal row for a bounded call names the full output and that the reference resolves after a process restart.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-migration-57-gap-fill-untested","category":"test_gap","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"No test covers applying migration 57 to a database already migrated through 58","claim":"Migration 57 is inserted into `MIGRATIONS` below migration 58, which already exists at the base revision — the change fills a numbering gap beneath an already-shipped migration. Every migration assertion the change touches counts or lists migrations applied to a freshly created (or hand-built legacy) database, where 57 is simply one more unapplied version; none constructs a database that has already recorded version 58 and then asserts that 57 is still applied and that `usage_observations` gains `edit_form_id`, `edit_form_version`, `truncation_config_id`, and `truncation_config_version`. If the applier ever selects migrations by comparing against the highest recorded version rather than by per-version membership, an already-upgraded production database silently skips 57 and every subsequent `append_observation` fails at runtime with a missing-column error, which no check in this plan would surface.","evidence":[{"kind":"diff_hunk","path":"crates/familiar-ai-storage/src/migrate.rs","hunk":"@@ -196,6 +196,10 @@ const MIGRATIONS: &[Migration] = &[\n         version: 56,\n         sql: include_str!(\"../migrations/056_substance_keyed_waivers.sql\"),\n     },\n+    Migration {\n+        version: 57,\n+        sql: include_str!(\"../migrations/057_token_discipline.sql\"),\n+    },\n     Migration {\n         version: 58,\n         sql: include_str!(\"../migrations/058_batch_reviews.sql\"),"},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e49bba884b456c5679ef7d301f615bae30cd474742a401bbcb30b9774f828160","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":75574,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-72","revision":"sha256:adfc1736954048d8d1721dca2833b5c983190caffd732fa102699977cf43f088","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e49bba884b456c5679ef7d301f615bae30cd474742a401bbcb30b9774f828160-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Add a migration test that seeds a database recorded as having applied every migration through 58 (without 57), runs `run_migrations`, and asserts the four new `usage_observations` columns exist and an `append_observation` round-trips. If the applier is max-version based, renumber this migration above 58 instead.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-retention-shared-temp-residual","category":"security_issue","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Retained tool output still sits under an attacker-influenceable shared-temp parent and is never removed","claim":"The 0700 directory check and 0600 file mode close the direct read exposure raised previously, but the retention root remains `std::env::temp_dir().join(\"familiar-ai-tool-output\")`, whose own creation via `create_dir_all` applies no ownership or permission requirement — only the per-execution child is verified and hardened. On a shared `/tmp`, another local user who pre-creates that parent owns the directory entry for every per-execution child beneath it: they can unlink the child the daemon just created and substitute a symlink, and `write_retention_file` opens with `OpenOptions` without `O_NOFOLLOW` or `O_EXCL`, so the daemon then truncates and writes command output through that symlink to a path of the attacker's choosing. The per-execution key is a SHA-256 of the worktree root plus the execution id, both values a local observer can derive. Separately, nothing in the change ever deletes retained files, so full command output accumulates under the temp root for the daemon's lifetime with no bound and no cleanup on execution completion.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","range":{"start":68,"end":168}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","range":{"start":309,"end":358}}],"remediation":"Move retention out of the shared system temp directory into a daemon-owned state directory the daemon creates and owns end to end (mirroring the worktree state root), verifying ownership and mode on the retention root as well as the per-execution child; open retention files with `O_NOFOLLOW`/`O_EXCL` so a substituted symlink fails closed; and delete an execution's retention directory when the execution reaches a terminal state.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-search-list-unbounded","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"low","blocking":false,"title":"`search-list` results are not bounded, so one tool result class still returns unbounded text to the model","claim":"Acceptance criterion 4 opens with \"Tool results returned to the model are bounded by default\" before naming the command-output and file-read cases. `execute` still dispatches `CapabilityId::SearchList` to `self.search_list(call)` unchanged — it receives neither the `AuthorityContext` nor any windowing, and `search_list` is untouched by this change. A `search-list` over a large tree therefore returns its full listing to the model even with token discipline enabled, leaving an input-volume path the discipline does not cover and no retention/paging handle for it.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","range":{"start":688,"end":700}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e49bba884b456c5679ef7d301f615bae30cd474742a401bbcb30b9774f828160","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":75574,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-72","revision":"sha256:adfc1736954048d8d1721dca2833b5c983190caffd732fa102699977cf43f088","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e49bba884b456c5679ef7d301f615bae30cd474742a401bbcb30b9774f828160-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Route `search_list` through the same `bound_tool_result` window and retention/paging path as `run_command` when token discipline is enabled, or state explicitly in the contract that `search-list` is out of scope for bounding and why.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-handle-path-traversal","category":"security_issue","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Prior finding: paging-handle path traversal in read-file","claim":"Fixed in this revision. The handle branch is now reached only when `token_discipline.enabled` (`self.token_discipline.enabled.then(|| tool_output_call_id(path)).flatten()`), so with discipline off every `read-file` path resolves through `resolve_within_worktree` exactly as before and a genuine worktree file named `.familiar/tool-output/<x>.txt` is no longer diverted. The extracted call id is validated by `is_safe_retention_call_id`, which rejects the empty string, `.`, `..`, and any value containing `/`, `\\`, or NUL, so the reported payload `.familiar/tool-output/../../../../../../etc/passwd.txt` yields a call id containing `/` and is refused before any path join. Both the retention directory and the resolved file are then canonicalized and the file is required to sit beneath the directory before any bytes are read. Two regression tests cover the traversal refusal and the discipline-disabled non-diversion.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","range":{"start":68,"end":168}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","range":{"start":309,"end":358}}],"remediation":"No further action; the confinement check, the enabled-gate, and the canonicalization guard are in place and covered by tests.","status":"resolved","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"td-retention-tempdir-exposure","category":"security_issue","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Prior finding: retained tool output exposed in the shared temp directory","claim":"Partially addressed and replaced. The direct read exposure is closed: `secure_retention_dir` now verifies the per-execution directory is a directory owned by the effective uid and chmods it to 0700 (re-reading to confirm), and `write_retention_file` creates the file with mode 0600, with a unix test asserting both modes. The remaining substance of this finding — the retention root still living under the shared system temp directory with no ownership requirement of its own, the symlink-substitution window that follows from an attacker-owned parent, and the complete absence of cleanup — is carried forward as `td-retention-shared-temp-residual`.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/agent_runtime.rs","range":{"start":68,"end":168}}],"remediation":"Track the residual exposure under `td-retention-shared-temp-residual`; the 0700/0600 hardening for the per-execution directory and its files needs no further change.","status":"superseded","supersedes":"td-retention-shared-temp-residual"}]}
